# beta_alanine.msf
# Beta-alanine (3-aminopropanoic acid)
# pKa1=3.550 (COOH), pKa2=10.240 (NH3+)
# Source: Perrin 1981 / NIST
# First non-alpha amino acid in the training set.
# The beta-position shifts pKa1 (3.55 vs alpha ~2.3) and lowers pKa2
# (10.24 vs alpha ~9.7) relative to alpha-amino acids, probing how well
# the model generalises amino acid charge patterns beyond alpha position.

